From eb78d0b5f4bbfec75b74ce017a891719a4d01b3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nau Fantom <353563530+nauxph@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:05:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix: Ocarina HUD flicker, green fog and movie sync on AMD

Local Lichii build for The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time (0400486024DEC000)
on an RX 9070 XT (AMD proprietary driver), on top of nx2 588bfa611b.

Ported pull requests:
- #292 bind compute table pointers up to 256 MiB. The fog classifier
  (75d4369f3b1f5868) reads its light probes ~110 MiB past their pointer.
  Past the 64 MiB cap NVIDIA read zeros (white haze) and AMD read garbage,
  which turned the sky, the fog and the water reflections neon green.
- #251 Ocarina movie clock: late decoded frames are skipped so movies keep
  time with their sound below 60 fps.
- #278 EDEN_NX2_FS_READ_MBPS: configurable IStorage read throttle (0 = off).
- #204 and #215: macro DMA reads wait for pending query results.
- #243 macro DMA reads on the split front without draining the back.
  EDEN_NX2_DMA_EARLY=0 turns the early reads off.
- #268 texture cache: large cards fill 5/8 of their budget before collecting.
- #259 opt-in EDEN_NX2_PREFLUSH=1.

Own changes:
- EDEN_NX2_RP_BARRIER=1: a full memory barrier before and after every render
  pass. Ocarina's minimap, hearts and dialogs vanished on about half of the
  frames on AMD although their draws ran in every frame (counted with
  EDEN_NX2_WATCH_SHADERS); with the barrier 0 of 40 frames lost them, at no
  visible frame-rate cost. Enabled through nx2_switches.txt; the exact
  missing dependency is still to be narrowed down.
- Draw texture blits now draw in the scheduler's render pass, keep the source
  image in GENERAL and invalidate the tracked state afterwards.
  EDEN_NX2_DRAW_TEXTURE_OLD=1 keeps the previous path.
- Fence acquires suspend the channel until the syncpoint is reached, giving
  up after 250 ms. EDEN_NX2_FENCE_WAIT=0 keeps the previous behaviour.
- Diagnostics: EDEN_NX2_WATCH_SHADERS (per-frame draw counts for the given
  shaders) and EDEN_NX2_IGNORE_RENDER_ENABLE.

